 tips on how  to go deathless  these deathless challenges are going to  be called  gauntlets of strength and they're going  to be single life challenges where if  you die you have to start over from the  beginning  we don't know what the gauntlets will  consist of exactly  maybe for example one challenge might  ask you to get to the end of the game  without dying  perhaps one of the gauntlets might ask  you to defeat all bosses  without dying or maybe a selection of  bosses without dying  but whatever these gauntlets consist of  we do know that they relate to bosses in  some way at least because  the devs want you to practice bosses for  these challenges  and we do know that there are at least  two types of gauntlet because  successfully completing one will reward  you with one  of three new cosmetic outfits they've  revealed that one of the reward outfits  is called tengu  another is called old ashina and the  third outfit  is something that's unlocked when you  simply beat the game once  now having outfits is one thing for the  replayability of the game  and it's something that pc players have  had access to for a really long time and  a lot of these outfits are really good  but it's another thing entirely to have  these skins  tied to challenges in game in my recent  stream  i actually mentioned exactly that i  talked about how the idea of tying skins  to a meaningful challenge  gives these games so much more  replayability and  from software delivered on that all we  needed was some sort of post-game  content to make this game  worth coming back to because just  thinking about the gameplay alone  secure is worth replaying mastering  bosses and mastering combat in this game  is kind of a thrill that no other souls  game can give you in my opinion you just  start to fight on a whole nother level  once you really practice this game  and i'm super excited to stream this  experience with you guys  next month yes it is weird that from  software are  updating sakura after a year and a half  of  nothing at all for this game but man  it's kind of smart in a way  for relatively little effort the game is  going to have  its online presence temporarily revived  on places like twitch and  a lot of people might be coming from  ghost of tsushima which was released  recently  and they might be looking for new things  to try  having one mode of difficulty in these  games does  really help the social experience of  playing this game  and sharing it with others because we're  all playing the exact same game  and we're connected by that fact but now  secure is  officially an online game with the new  edition of  remnants so according to the blog post  remnants are recordings of what a player  does in game for up to 30 seconds at a  time  and they're available for use after the  game's tutorial after a player records  their remnant  whether it's an epic takedown of an  enemy or a flawless demonstration of a  tricky movement technique  it can be uploaded with a written  message so that other community members  can play it back  so for those seeking guidance on how to  beat something or looking for hidden  items  the hope is that these records might  prove a blessing  and if a community member watches one of  your remnants and then rates it  the owner will have their hp recovered  for free which allows you to get back  into the fight  without having to heal or rest at a  sculptor's idol  so this is the sort of addition that  does make sekido a bit more  accessible to new players it's not much  but with this  new players might be able to see what  experienced players are doing to succeed  and they might be able to see what  inexperienced players are doing to fail  in the recent video we also talked about  how sakura could use more stuff like  this  and it's one that makes the game online  no less  for a long time sakura pc has actually  had a really good  online mod it adds co-op and pvp to the  game which  is an amazing community creation and  it's super fun with your friends  but there are definitely moments in this  mod that made me understand why they  made secure  a single player experience so finally  what does this mean for the future of  the ip they announced that the game has  sold more than 5 million copies now  and it convincingly won game of the year  last year  it's also really well primed for dlc or  sequel content  based on the character tomaway or  regarding the  journey to the west that's referenced in  one of the endings  so the question we have to ask now is  are these quality of life additions to  the game  just a way to temporarily revive it or  are they something more regardless  subscribe and stay tuned  also check out our sakura inspired merch  that went live last week  i've temporarily made the limited red  kanji edition  available again for a couple of days so  if you need a new hoodie or a new  t-shirt go and check it out  in the description thanks for watching  and i'll see you back in sakura  on october 29th  you
 

